cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Early prediction of acute treatment escalation in the ICU: analysis code
message: >-
  If you use this code or build on the measurement-behaviour decomposition,
  please cite both the software and the thesis.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Maloth
    given-names: Shivaprasad
    affiliation: SRH University of Applied Sciences Heidelberg
repository-code: 'https://github.com/Maloth04/Early-Prediction-of-Patient-Deterioration-in-the-ICU-An-Explainable-ML-Study-on-MIMIC-IV-and-eICU-'
abstract: >-
  Analysis code for a Master's thesis on early prediction of a composite
  acute-escalation endpoint in MIMIC-IV v2.2, at four- and eight-hour horizons
  from a 24-hour observation window. Its contribution is a reporting procedure:
  a feature block recording only measurement behaviour, with no clinical values,
  is reported alongside the full model, and recovers roughly three quarters of
  above-chance discrimination on its own. Geographic external validation was not
  delivered and no transport claim is made.
keywords:
  - clinical deterioration
  - intensive care
  - clinical prediction model
  - explainability
  - informative missingness
  - MIMIC-IV
